\**{c=red:Note for Windower and Ashita users:}** The last cutscene will most likely freeze. This happens even at the default framerate. If this happens, the Mission will still be flagged as completed, and you can continue to the next Mission after disconnecting and logging in again.
If you wish to watch the cutscene, disconnect from the game and log in without Windower.
You can restart the cutscene from the {p:Goblin Footprint} at (K-6/7) by trading it an item or Gil, which will be returned to you.
=2 Walkthrough
* Interact with the **Outcropping** at (F-10) in {z:Gustav Tunnel} for a cutscene.
** {p:Unity Warp} 128 from {z:Cape Teriggan} can be faster for those without movement speed bonuses.
** {p:Survival Guide} in {z:Gustav Tunnel} (K-7) puts you on the opposite end of the tunnel. You will not need {s:Sneak} at level 75.
* The following fight is trivial at level cap, but if you're at a lower level, prepare to battle:
* Interacting with the **Outcropping** again will start a fight against 3 Tenshodo agents named {m:Renfred}, {m:Bompupu} and {m:Gorattz} and consume the {@k} {k:Black book} Key Item.
** {p:Trust Magic} can not be used in this fight.
** You will keep your buffs: {p:Phalanx} will negate all damage from this fight except {m:Bompupu}'s nukes.
* The 3 agents start off untargetable and cast {p:Utsusemi: Ni} a few times, then 4 clones of each will spawn.
** The clones aren't very strong, having low HP, accuracy, attack and defense, and cast elemental and enfeebling Ninjutsu.
* At some point (either time elapsed or number of clones defeated), the 3 agents will join the fight, at which time they can be attacked, and must be defeated in order to win the encounter.
** They can be differentiated from the clones because they have higher HP and will continue to cast Utsusemi as well as other Ninjutsu.
** Once in the fight, they will still continue to spawn clones as the clones are dispatched.
** Once an agent is defeated, any of his or her remaining clones will despawn after a couple of seconds.
* When all 3 agents are down, you will be rewarded a {@k} {k:Cactuar key}, which can be redeemed at the {p:Treasure Coffer|Add-on Scenario Rewards} in **Tenshodo Headquarters** in {z:Lower Jeuno}.
* Interact with the **Outcropping** again for a cutscene.

=2 "A Shantotto Ascension" Key
* After completing the mission, the activity is repeatable for an additional reward once per day.
** Augmented equipment is a common reward but there is also crafting ingredients and spell scrolls.
* Re-obtain a {@k} {k:Black book} in {z:Norg} by bringing the requested {i:Soul Plates|Soul Plate|2477} as you did in {M:the previous mission|A Shantotto Ascension Mission 5|Enemy of the Empire (I)}.
** Alternatively, the {k:Black book} Key Item can be purchased from {n:Squintrox Dryeyes} for 500g and 5 {i:Beastmen's Seals|Beastmen's Seal|1126} after all {p:A Shantotto Ascension Missions|Category:A Shantotto Ascension Missions} are completed.
* Travel to {z:Gustav Tunnel} and examine the **Outcropping** (F-10) to begin the battle with the Tenshodo.
* When you've defeated all three agents, you will receive another {@k} {k:Cactuar key},
** The key can be received once per day.
* Go to {z:Lower Jeuno} and enter the **{p:Tenshodo} HQ**.
* Interact with the red treasure coffer at (J-8) and use the {@k} {k:Cactuar key} (Level 50) to receive the reward.
** Rewards are listed on the {p:Add-on Scenario Rewards} page.

